Matthew Cline <matt_newz@sbcglobal.net> wrote:
>Why *can't* you wish for a magic lamp?  A blessed magic lamp only gives you an 
>80% chance of a wish, so it's like taking a 20% chance of a wish not working 
>in return for a permanent light source.  You can wish for powerful things 
>like various gauntlets, dragon scale mail, and such, even artifacts; is a 
>permanent light source that much more powerful/useful that you shouldn't be 
>able to wish for it.

No... but as it stands, if you only find one magic lamp, you can have 1500
turns of light and an 80% chance of a wish *or* you can have permanent
light.  There are other sources of wishes, if you live long enough or get
lucky with fountains and potions; there is no other source of permanent
light (except for Sunsword, but you have to wield it to get the benefit).

If you could wish for magic lamps, it becomes almost trivially the case
that an early magic lamp should always be blessed and #rubbed in pursuit
of that 80% chance of a wish, since you still get your 1500 turns of light
and can wish for a permanent light later on.  This makes the game less
interesting by essentially eliminating a currently significant tradeoff
between tactics ("get the wish! now!" is more tactically sound) and
strategy ("keep the lamp, and burn it for a wish if you find another" is
more strategically sound, if you can survive without the wish).

